        {
          "id": 603327714,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There is still a warning emitted so anyone can fix that.\n\nNote that the errors are almost always not related to the code one is working on. So this doesn't help prevent warnings from appearing in the master branch (because they will not appear with -O2, which is what the build bots use), the error is just a massive inconvenience to everyone else who gets whacked in the head with it and has to deal with the error in the middle of a completely different task. An error for code they didn't introduce or touch.\n\nWhat happens in that situation is that variables are simply set to zero to be initialized and silent the warning, instead of really trying to understand if it is a legitimate issue or not, and nothing gets fixed, it's just papered over.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-06-16T19:51:02.399Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-06-16T19:51:02.399Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 104325085,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
